{
  "name": "Review Standards (Manual)",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Manually trigger a review of the currently active file against project standards.",
  "enabled": true,
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Review the currently active/open file against these project standards and report any violations. Do NOT auto-fix, only report issues.\n\nStandards to check:\n1. No locators inside test files (test_*.py). All selectors must live in page objects.\n2. No manual waits (time.sleep). Rely on Playwright auto-wait.\n3. No hardcoded test data in test files.\n4. Page objects must inherit from BasePageSelenium or BasePagePlaywright.\n5. Prefer stable locators (data-testid, ids, aria labels) over brittle XPath.\n6. Minimize print usage. Rely on assertion messages and Allure reporting.\n7. Test naming must follow: test_[action]_[condition]_[expected_result].\n8. No duplicated code. Reusable actions belong in base page or page objects.\n9. Page object classes should be under ~200 lines.\n\nIf the file is clean, say so briefly. Only detail violations if there are any."
  }
}
